PART 1 — WHAT I FOUND (audit of the aiteam folder at d5d5e2b)
================================================================================

HEADLINE: HEAD was dead on arrival. studio.py could not even be imported.
Line 266 read:

    def save_memorydef save_memory(text):

…a botched edit from the 18:15 "Fix Audit5" commit (d5d5e2b), pushed 5 minutes
before I cloned. Everything downstream (studio.py AND gui.py, which imports
studio for export_build + detectors) was broken. The system that passed Audit 5
at ad28b75 had been broken by the very commits claiming to finish it.

Findings, by severity:

[BROKEN AT IMPORT]
F1  Line 266 SyntaxError (above). py_compile fails → nothing runs. Introduced
    by d5d5e2b; 15c4ef2 had it right.

[CRITICAL — infinite loop, worse than anything left from Audit 5]
F2  The "H1a fix" in the parallel lane was itself a new infinite loop.
    process_one_task() returned status "skipped_breaker" for attempts>=3, but
    the results loop only knew two branches: failed (res None) or done. A
    breaker-skipped task was marked "failed" — and "failed" tasks are re-selected
    as pending every cycle. Result: the same task was re-dispatched, instantly
    re-skipped, and re-failed in a ~2-second tight loop FOREVER, with no log
    line explaining it. The audit-5 "bounded loop" fix created an unbounded one.
F3  Double attempt-counting in the parallel lane: attempts was incremented
    pre-call inside process_one_task AND again on success in the results loop,
    so a first-time parallel task ended with attempts=2 — corrupting every
    downstream "< 3" retry guard.
F4  The dead second cap block (H3/N4b) was still present — THREE consecutive
    commit messages claimed it deleted. It sat after the `if not pending:`
    guard, so pending_count==0 could never be true there: unreachable code.
    (Note: my first two removal attempts here clipped neighboring lines — the
    block was re-seated, indentation-corrected, and re-verified; see Part 3.)

[CRITICAL — language misdetection at the core of the system]
F5  The C++ / C# regexes could never match. r"\bc\+\+\b" demands a word
    boundary after '+' — '+' is a non-word char, so the boundary cannot exist.
    Same class of bug for 'c#'. Consequence: "LANGUAGE: C++" silently fell
    through to Python. Proven by test, then PROVEN FIXED with an 11-case matrix.
F6  No-LANGUAGE-field GDDs silently built Python even when the GDD text said
    another engine/language. The shipped 5. GDD.md has NO LANGUAGE field (it
    says "Godot 4.2 GDScript (preferred) or Unity C#") — so the shipped default
    project would have been planned/built as Python.

[HIGH]
F7  M6 regex was still eating legitimate title words: the suffix strip ran
    with IGNORECASE, so _Cafe, _Fade, _Face, _Deed, _Bead (all in [a-f]) were
    consumed. The "fix" that moved the strip before _->space fixed the ordering
    but not the case problem. Real world hit: '07_spark_Boss_Beef_Cafe' →
    'boss beef'.
F8  M7 similarity dedup STILL absent (claimed in 2+ commit messages): pure
    containment, which over-blocks ('save system' present → 'Save System Cloud
    Sync', 'Autosave System' and even 'System' all skipped as "duplicates").
F9  <think>-block leak resurrected in the .md fallback of BOTH worker paths:
    when extraction produced <50 chars, the code fell back to the RAW LLM
    response — the raw response still carries deepseek-r1's <think> reasoning
    blocks (the extractor's stripped text was discarded). Comment on the line
    said "<think> already stripped". It was not. GLITCH QA files polluted again.
F10 AURA's memory slice read the FIRST 2500 chars of MEMORY, so as memory grew
    the most recent completions never reached the planner; and the in-process
    memory_summary string grew unbounded for the life of the process.

[MEDIUM]
F11 Integrator had its own THIRD copy of the code-fence extraction logic
    (besides the canonical extractor and… itself twice), already drifted.
F12 ensure_build_runnable's WARNING claimed "LLM output empty or too short
    (<=10 chars)" in cases where that was false, and the Python fallback text
    pointed users at repo_backup/ — a folder that does not exist (audit L8).
F13 Per Audit 5's H2-ollama: no /api/tags preflight (a missing model surfaced
    only as a burned task attempt), and no per-role inference settings.
F14 gui.py: BASE not resolve()'d (CWD-dependent paths — audit N2-analog), no
    restore path for the output backups Fresh Start creates, and a malformed
    needs-code filename for non-Python languages ('[:2]' slice → ".py" for C++).

